        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55601",
          "text": "<p>The postfix expression AB + CD -* can be evaluated using a</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>stack</li>\n    <li>tree</li>\n    <li>queue</li>\n    <li>linked list</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2,data-structures,stack,infix-prefix",
          "category": "Data Structures"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55603",
          "text": "<p>The post order traversal of a binary tree is DEBFCA. Find out the pre-order traversal</p><ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>ABFCDE</li><li>ADBFEC</li><li>ABDECF</li><li>None of the above</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2,algorithms,binary-tree",
          "category": "Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55604",
          "text": "<p>The branch logic that provides decision making capabilities in the control unit is known as</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>Controlled transfer</li>\n    <li>Conditional transfer</li>\n    <li>Unconditional transfer</li>\n    <li>None of the above</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2,co-and-architecture",
          "category": "CO & Architecture"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55606",
          "text": "\n<p>The number of colours required to properly colour the vertices of every planer graph is</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>2</li>\n    <li>3</li>\n    <li>4</li>\n    <li>5</li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2,graph-theory,graph-coloring",
          "category": "Graph Theory"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55607",
          "text": "\n<p>Networks that use different technologies can be connected by using</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>Packets</li>\n    <li>Switches</li>\n    <li>Bridges</li>\n    <li>Routers</li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2,computer-networks",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55608",
          "text": "\n<p>Both hosts and routers and TCP/IP protocol software. However, routers do not use protocol from all layers. The layer for which the protocol software is not needed by a router is</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>Layer &ndash; 5 (Application)</li>\n    <li>Layer &ndash; 1 (Physical)</li>\n    <li>Layer &ndash; 3 (Internet)</li>\n    <li>Layer &ndash; 4 (Network Interface)</li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2,computer-networks,network-layering",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55611",
          "text": "\n<p>In multiuser database if two users wish to update the same record at the same time, they are prevented from doing so by</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>Jamming</li>\n    <li>Password</li>\n    <li>Documentation</li>\n    <li>Record lock</li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2,databases",
          "category": "Databases"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55613",
          "text": "\n<p>A binary search tree is a binary tree in which</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>All items in the left subtree are less than root</li>\n    <li>All items in the right subtree are greater than or equal to root</li>\n    <li>Each subtree is itself a binary search tree</li>\n    <li>All of the above</li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2,data-structures,binary-tree",
          "category": "Data Structures"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55614",
          "text": "<p>What deletes the entire file except the file structure?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>ERASE</li>\n    <li>DELETE</li>\n    <li>ZAP</li>\n    <li>PACK</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2,databases,non-gatecse",
          "category": "Web Technologies"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55615",
          "text": "\n<p>Which command is the fastest among the following?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>COPY TO &lt;NEW FILE&gt;</li>\n    <li>COPY STRUCTURE TO &lt;NEW FILE&gt;</li>\n    <li>COPY FILE &lt;FILE 1&gt; &lt;FILE 2&gt;</li>\n    <li>COPY TO MFILE-DAT DELIMITED</li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2,operating-system,file-system",
          "category": "Operating System"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "646",
          "text": "\n<p>B$^{+}$-trees are preferred to binary trees in databases because</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>Disk capacities are greater than memory capacities</li>\n    <li>Disk access is much slower than memory access</li>\n    <li>Disk data transfer rates are much less than memory data transfer rates</li>\n    <li>Disks are more reliable than memory</li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "gatecse-2000,databases,b-tree,normal,ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2",
          "category": "Databases"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55616",
          "text": "\n<p>A Transaction Manager is which of the following?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>Maintains a log of transactions</li>\n    <li>Maintains before and after database images</li>\n    <li>Maintains appropriate concurrent control</li>\n    <li>All of the above</li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2,databases,transaction-and-concurrency",
          "category": "Databases"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "50682",
          "text": "Leaves of which of the following trees are at the same level?\n\nA.    Binary tree\nB.    B-tree\nC.    AVL-tree\nD.    Expression tree",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2,programming,tree",
          "category": "Data Structures"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55617",
          "text": "\n<p>Which of the following TCP/IP Internet protocol does diskless machine uses to obtain its IP address from a server?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>RAP</li>\n    <li>RIP</li>\n    <li>ARP</li>\n    <li>X.25</li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "x",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2,computer-networks",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55834",
          "text": "\n<p>Decryption and encryption of data are responsibility of which of the following layer?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>Physical layer</li>\n    <li>Data link layer</li>\n    <li>Presentation layer</li>\n    <li>Session layer</li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2,computer-networks,network-layering",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55835",
          "text": "\n<p>In which circuit switching, delivery of data is delayed because data must be stored and retrieved from RAM?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>Space division</li>\n    <li>Time division</li>\n    <li>Virtual</li>\n    <li>Packet</li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "B",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2,computer-networks,network-switching",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55837",
          "text": "\n<p>&nbsp;In which routing method do all the routers have a common database?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>Distance vector</li>\n    <li>Link state</li>\n    <li>Link vector</li>\n    <li>Dijikstra method</li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2,computer-networks,routing",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55838",
          "text": "\n<p>Page Shift Keying (PSK) Method is used to modulate digital signal at 9600 bps using 16 level. Find the line signals and speed (i.e., modulation rate)</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>2400 bauds</li>\n    <li>1200 bauds</li>\n    <li>4800 bauds</li>\n    <li>9600 bauds</li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2,non-gatecse,digital-signal-processing",
          "category": "Digital Signal Processing"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55839",
          "text": "\n<p>The station to hub distance in which it is 2000 meters</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>100 Base-T$_X$</li>\n    <li><span style=\"line-height: 1.6;\">100 Base-F$_X$</span></li>\n    <li><span style=\"line-height: 1.6;\">100 Base-T$_4$</span></li>\n    <li><span style=\"line-height: 1.6;\">100 Base-T$_1$</span></li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2,computer-networks,communication",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55840",
          "text": "\n<p>Main aim of software engineering is to produce</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>program</li>\n    <li>software</li>\n    <li>within budget</li>\n    <li>software within budget in the given schedule&nbsp;</li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2,non-gatecse,is&software-engineering",
          "category": "IS&Software Engineering"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55842",
          "text": "\n<p>Key process areas of CMM level 4 are also classified by a process which is</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>CMM level 2</li>\n    <li>CMM level 3</li>\n    <li>CMM level 5</li>\n    <li>All of the above</li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2,non-gatecse,is&software-engineering",
          "category": "IS&Software Engineering"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55843",
          "text": "\n<p>Validation means</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>are we building the product right</li>\n    <li>are we building the right product</li>\n    <li>verification of fields</li>\n    <li>None of the above</li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2,is&software-engineering,non-gatecse",
          "category": "IS&Software Engineering"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55844",
          "text": "\n<p>&nbsp;If a process is under statistical control, then it is</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>Maintainable</li>\n    <li>Measurable</li>\n    <li>Predictable</li>\n    <li>Verifiable</li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2,non-gatecse,is&software-engineering",
          "category": "IS&Software Engineering"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55845",
          "text": "\n<p>&nbsp;In a function oriented design, we</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>minimize cohesion and maximize coupling</li>\n    <li>maximize cohesion and minimize coupling</li>\n    <li>maximize cohesion and maximize coupling</li>\n    <li>minimize cohesion and minimize coupling</li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2,non-gatecse,is&software-engineering",
          "category": "IS&Software Engineering"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55846",
          "text": "\n<p>&nbsp;Which of the following metric does not depend on the programming language used?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>Line of code</li>\n    <li>Function count</li>\n    <li>Member of token</li>\n    <li>All of the above</li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "non-gatecse,is&software-engineering,ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2",
          "category": "IS&Software Engineering"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "853",
          "text": "<p>A $B^+$ - tree index is to be built on the <em>Name</em>&nbsp;attribute of the relation&nbsp;<em>STUDENT.&nbsp;</em>Assume that all the student names are of length $8$ bytes, disk blocks are of size $512$ bytes, and index pointers are of size $4$ bytes. Given the scenario, what would be the best choice of the degree (i.e. number of pointers per node) of the $B^+$ - tree?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$16$</li>\n    <li>$42$</li>\n    <li>$43$</li>\n    <li>$44$</li>\n</ol>\n\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "gatecse-2002,databases,b-tree,normal,ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2",
          "category": "Databases"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55849",
          "text": "<p>The Inorder traversal of the tree will yield a sorted listing of elements of tree in</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>Binary tree</li>\n    <li>Binary search tree</li>\n    <li>Heaps</li>\n    <li>None of the above</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "data-structures,binary-tree,ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2",
          "category": "Data Structures"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "45089",
          "text": "<p>Mobile IP provides two basic functions</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>Route discovery and registration</li>\n    <li>Agent discovery and registration</li>\n    <li>IP binding and registration</li>\n    <li>None of the above</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2,computer-networks,mobile-communication,wireless-communication",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55863",
          "text": "\n<p>Pre-emptive scheduling is the strategy of temporarily suspending a running process</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>before the CPU time slice expires</li>\n    <li>to allow starving processes to run</li>\n    <li>when it requires I/O</li>\n    <li>to avoid collision</li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "operating-system,process-scheduling,ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2",
          "category": "Operating System"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "46841",
          "text": "\n<p style=\"line-height: 20.8px;\">In round robin CPU scheduling as time quantum is increased the average turn around time</p>\n\n<ol style=\"line-height: 20.8px; list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>increases</li>\n    <li>decreases</li>\n    <li>remains constant</li>\n    <li>varies irregularly</li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2,operating-system,process-scheduling",
          "category": "Operating System"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55866",
          "text": "\n<p>&nbsp;Resources are allocated to the process on non-sharable basis is</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>mutual exclusion</li>\n    <li>hold and wait</li>\n    <li>no pre-emption</li>\n    <li>circular wait</li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2,operating-system,resource-allocation",
          "category": "Operating System"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "45088",
          "text": "<p>Cached and interleaved memories are ways of speeding up memory access between CPU’s and slower RAM. Which memory models are best suited (i.e. improves the performance most) for which programs ?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-roman\">\n    <li>Cached memory is best suited for small loops.</li>\n    <li>Interleaved memory is best suited for small loops</li>\n    <li>Interleaved memory is best suited for large sequential code.</li>\n    <li>Cached memory is best suited for large sequential code.\n    <ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n        <li>I and II are true</li>\n        <li>I and III are true</li>\n        <li>IV and II are true</li>\n        <li>IV and III are true</li>\n    </ol>\n    </li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2,co-and-architecture,cache-memory",
          "category": "CO & Architecture"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55870",
          "text": "\n<p>Consider the following page trace:</p>\n\n<p>4,3,2,1,4,3,5,4,3,2,1,5</p>\n\n<p>Percentage of page fault that would occur if FIFO page replacement algorithm is used with number of frames for the JOB m=4 will be</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>8</li>\n    <li>9</li>\n    <li>10</li>\n    <li>12</li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "operating-system,page-replacement,ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2",
          "category": "Operating System"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55876",
          "text": "\n<p>Checksum used along with each packet computes the sum of the data, where data is treated as a sequence of</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>Integer</li>\n    <li>Character</li>\n    <li>Real numbers</li>\n    <li>Bits</li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "computer-networks,ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55878",
          "text": "\n<p>If an integer needs two bytes of storage, then the maximum value of signed integer is</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>$2^{16}-1$</li>\n    <li><span style=\"line-height: 1.6;\">$2^{15}-1$</span></li>\n    <li><span style=\"line-height: 1.6;\">$2^{16}$</span></li>\n    <li><span style=\"line-height: 1.6;\">$2^{15}$</span></li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "digital-logic,number-representation,ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55879",
          "text": "\n<p>Which of the following logic families is well suited for high-speed operations?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>TTL</li>\n    <li>ECL</li>\n    <li>MOS</li>\n    <li>CMOS</li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "non-gatecse,integrated-circuits,ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2",
          "category": "Integrated Circuits"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55881",
          "text": "\n<p>Interrupts which are initiated by an instruction are</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>Internal</li>\n    <li>External</li>\n    <li>Hardware</li>\n    <li>Software</li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "co-and-architecture,interrupts,ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2",
          "category": "CO & Architecture"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55882",
          "text": "\n<p>printf(&ldquo;%c&rdquo;, 100);</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>prints 100</li>\n    <li>prints ASCII equivalent of 100</li>\n    <li>prints &nbsp;garbage</li>\n    <li>None of the above</li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "non-gatecse,programming-in-c,ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2",
          "category": "Programming in C"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55883",
          "text": "\n<p>For the transmission of the signal. Bluetooth wireless technology uses</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>time division multiplexing</li>\n    <li>frequency division multiplexing</li>\n    <li>time division duplex</li>\n    <li>frequency division duplex</li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "computer-networks,communication,ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55885",
          "text": "\n<p>&nbsp;Consider the following statements:</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-roman;\"><li>Recursive languages are closed under complementation</li>\n    <li>Recursively enumerable languages are closed under union</li>\n    <li>Recursively enumerable languages are closed under complementation</li>\n</ol><p>Which of the above statements are true?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>I only</li>\n    <li>I and II</li>\n    <li>I and III</li>\n    <li>II and III</li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "theory-of-computation,closure-property,ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2",
          "category": "Theory of Computation"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55886",
          "text": "\n<p>&nbsp;What is the routing algorithm used by RIP and IGRP?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>OSPF</li>\n    <li>Link-state</li>\n    <li>Dynamic</li>\n    <li>Dijikstra vector</li>\n</ol>\n",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "computer-networks,routing,ugcnetcse-june2012-paper2",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "55887",
          "text": "<p>Identify the incorrect statement:</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>The overall strategy drives the E-Commerce data warehousing strategy</li>\n    <li>Data warehousing in an E-Commerce environment should be done in classical manner</li>\n    <li>E-Commerce opens up and entirely new world web server</li>\n    <li>E-Commerce security threats can be grouped into three major categories</li>\n</ol>",
